01:48.456 --> 01:50.356
Well, that's impossible,
even for a computer.

01:50.458 --> 01:53.985
It's not impossible. I used to bullseye
womp rats in my T-16 back home.

01:54.095 --> 01:56.461
They're not much bigger than two meters.

01:56.598 --> 01:59.864
Hey, can I talk to you
privately for a second?

01:59.969 --> 02:01.095
Sure.

02:02.071 --> 02:04.835
That was unnecessary.

02:04.940 --> 02:07.534
- What's the problem?
- Well, you just kind of called me out

02:07.643 --> 02:10.544
- in front of everybody back there.
- I was just making a point.

02:10.646 --> 02:13.275
I know, but you like
just kind of sandbagged me

02:13.383 --> 02:14.350
in front of everyone we know.

02:14.451 --> 02:15.975
- Oh, I "sandbagged" you?
- In front of all of our friends.

02:16.086 --> 02:17.576
- Yeah, you sandbagged me.
- I "sandbagged" you?

02:17.687 --> 02:18.915
You sandbagged me, yes.

02:19.022 --> 02:20.614
Well, here I am trying to help you
with something...

02:20.724 --> 02:23.090
You know what,
I don't need your kind of help, all right?

02:23.193 --> 02:25.389
Have a great assault. Jerk.

02:35.873 --> 02:38.741
Lois, I don't understand
why I got to sit through a chick flick.

02:38.844 --> 02:41.745
<i>Peter, you promised you'd come with me
to see Autumn's Piano.</i>

02:41.847 --> 02:44.407
Besides, you owe me big
after the way you embarrassed me

02:44.516 --> 02:45.505
